\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Weakens Early As Market Eyes Rate Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2009\par 13:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real weakened in early trading Monday as investors mulled the increasing likelihood of declining interest rates locally.\par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL2.320 per dollar after ending at BRL2.313 on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange Friday.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted investors were keeping a cautious stance, shifting expectations over local interest rates. According to a weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  market survey released Monday, the bank is seen lowering the country's reference Selic interest rate to 13.25% by the end of the month from 13.75% currently under the effects of slowing domestic economic activity.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary policy committee is scheduled to meet Jan. 21 to decide on whether to alter the rate. The committee has held the rate unchanged since September as it evaluates the threat of accelerated inflation.\par \par \uc2 The local market also continues to be affected by thin liquidity as reduced numbers of investors participated in the market during the prolongation of year-end holidays.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, is seen possibly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with a spot market dollar sale. The bank has sold dollars from foreign reserves regularly at daily auctions since September to limit volatility.\par \par \uc2 As of Friday, foreign reserves stood at $207 billion.\par \par \uc2 According to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  market survey released Monday, the real is seen averaging BRL2.25 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real has fallen about 30% against the dollar since August in reaction to investor risk aversion prompted by tight credit markets and an accompanying global economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 05-01-09 1228GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090105e515000dk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
