\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Ends Weaker On Outflows, No Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2008\par 20:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real slid late in the session Thursday to end weaker against the dollar, in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local markets and influence from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflows.\par \par \uc2 The real ended at BRL2.280 per dollar after ending at BRL2.267 on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted that the real held steady against the dollar for most of the session as investors took encouragement with upbeat market signals from European exchanges during the U.S. Thanksgiving holiday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wavered somewhat as local equities slipped on doubts raised about alleged cash-flow difficulties by state-controlled oil giant \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  (PBR).\par \par \uc2 The market was also affected by local bank Unibanco's announcemnt (UBB) announcement late Wednesday that it planned a buyout of its local insurance partnership with AIG (AIG) for $820 million.\par \par \uc2 The real held ground until late in the day, but slumped as investors confirmed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  opted not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market with a customary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auction. The bank has injected local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures market more than $30 billion in swaps over the past two months in an effort to offer liquidity in the face of tight global credit.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in local interest rate futures trading, rates were slightly higher amid a continued focus on accelerated domestic inflation.\par \par \uc2 The rate on the most heavily traded futures contract, January 2010, ended at 14.64% after closing at 14.61% Wednesday. Brazil's interbank overnight rate ended unchanged at 13.17%.\par \par \uc2 During the session Thursday, Brazil's treasury sold BRL650 million in fixed-rate LTN bonds at average interest rates of 13.98% and 15.47% on bonds coming due in 2009 and 2011.\par \par \uc2 The treasury also reported it sold BRL500 million in March 2011 LFT floating-rate bonds at a premium of 0.0100%.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 27-11-08 1914GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081127e4br000vl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
