\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Stronger On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2008\par 19:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed stronger against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollar swap contracts in two separate auctions.\par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.275 per dollar, stronger against the Tuesday close of BRL2.325.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a total of $1.01 billion in dollar swap contracts at two separate auctions Wednesday. The auctions allow investors to build dollar positions by swapping government paper linked to interest rates for paper linked to the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Typically, the auctions strengthen the Brazilian real by creating options for investors to hold U.S. dollar positions.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted there was little volume in Wednesday's market, with many investors sidelined ahead of the U.S. Thanksgiving holiday Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In Brazilian credit markets, investors were heartened by government figures showing a robust primary budget surplus in October. The government rolled up a surplus of BRL14.47 billion, up from BRL10.0 billion in September.\par \par \uc2 The budget figures will help Brazil meet fiscal austerity targets and hold down inflation and interest rates.\par \par \uc2 On the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, all interest rate futures contracts closed lower Wednesday. The contracts reflect investor expectations about annualized interest rates at future dates.\par \par \uc2 The most actively traded interest rate futures contract, that of January 2010, closed at 14.57%, down from 14.67% Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 -By Tom Murphy, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-2847-4519; brazil@dowjones.com [ 26-11-08 1832GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081126e4bq000t0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
