\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Ends Stronger As  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Derivative Fears Fade\b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2008\par 19:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real strengthened against the U.S. dollar Tuesday on news a leading Brazilian exporter had negotiated an agreement with banks over its dollar derivative debts.\par \par \uc2 The real closed sharply stronger at BRL2.110 per dollar on the Brazilian Mercantile & Futures Exchange, or BM&F, against the Monday close of BRL2.1670.\par \par \uc2 The real traded stronger throughout Tuesday after major Brazilian pulp and paper exporting giant \uc2 Aracruz Celulose SA\uc2  (ARA) said that it had agreed with a group of banks to liquidate 97% of its positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives contracts. The contracts generated estimated losses of $2.1 billion.\par \par \uc2 The solution to the \uc2 Aracruz\uc2  derivatives problem was welcomed by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders because the company had been the subject of daily commentaries - and blamed by some for market volatility in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 Aracruz\uc2  hit the headlines in early October when it said that it held negative positions of BRL1.95 billion ($928 million) in derivatives markets as of Sept. 30, following the sharp depreciation of the real against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real also benefitted from the good humor of the local stock market, which traded increasingly higher through most of Tuesday. The Ibovespa stock index traded above the psychologically important 40,000-point barrier in late afternoon trading.\par \par \uc2 Investors were showing a reduced aversion to risk with banking stocks doing particularly well, after the announced planned merger of Banco Itau (ITA) and Unibanco (UBB). The merger will create Brazil's largest private bank and increase confidence in the solidity of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's banking system.\par \par \uc2 The real also benefited from continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Central bankers continued to defend the real Tuesday, with a scheduled dollar swap auction in the afternoon, selling $601.1 million.\par \par \uc2 Swaps allow investors with Brazilian interest rate-linked bonds to exchange them for positions in dollar-linked paper, thus easing pressure on the real in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 Interest rate futures contracts on the BM&F also reflected improved investor sentiment, closing mostly lower. The contracts reflect investor expectations for interest rates at future dates.\par \par \uc2 The most actively traded contract, January 2010, closed at 15.27%, down from 15.56% Monday. The overnight interbank rate, known as the CDI, closed lower at 13.58%, down from Monday's close at 13.63%.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the risk to investing in Brazil as measured by the \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus, or EMBI+, tightened slightly to a spread of 437 basis points over U.S. Treasurys. Brazil's benchmark Global 40 bond was 2 3/16 higher at a bid of 119 1/2.\par \par \uc2 -By John Kolodziejski, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-2586-6086; john.kolodziejski@dowjones.com [ 04-11-08 1833GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081104e4b400109\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
