\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Weaker Despite Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2008\par 20:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real lost ground again Friday against the U.S. dollar despite persistent government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.327 per dollar, weaker against the Thursday close of BRL2.305.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the real weakened as foreign investors continued to pull up stakes in Brazilian assets. Meanwhile, local banks and investment funds continued to build U.S. dollar positions in the face of turbulent local and international market conditions.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on four different occasions during the day Friday.\par \par \uc2 Twice, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollar swap contracts. The contracts offer investors \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  protection through contracts linked to the U.S. dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sold dollars directly to the market at two separate auctions, one in the morning and one in the afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was enough to prevent wild swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday, traders said.\par \par \uc2 In credit markets, investors were also nervous Friday on worries that the global credit crunch could severely restrict credit availability in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 Interest rate futures contracts on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange closed higher across the board. The contracts reflect investor expectations for interest rates at future dates.\par \par \uc2 The most actively traded contract, that of January 2010, closed at 16.85%, up from 16.00% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 -By Tom Murphy, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-2847-4519; brazil@dowjones.com [ 24-10-08 1838GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081024e4ao000v5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
