\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Ends Stronger After Heavy Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2008\par 20:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed sharply higher against the U.S. dollar Thursday, after \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to reverse an early slide.\par \par \uc2 The real ended at BRL2.3050 to the dollar, markedly stronger against Wednesday's close of BRL2.3795.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real plunged on opening Thursday, weakening to BRL2.532 in early trading, before Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reacted to stimulate a strong rally.\par \par \uc2 The bank's first action, an hour after trading began, was to announce a $50 billion long-term program of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap sales.\par \par \uc2 This was followed by two direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the dollar spot market, in quick succession, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling dollars to investors. A third sales auction came just before the market closed.\par \par \uc2 In the third auction, the bank sold dollars on the spot market for BRL2.2600. The bank gave no information on who bought them nor how many dollars were sold.\par \par \uc2 "In a time of low-level market confidence, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to hit hard...It had to do what it did today," a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialist said.\par \par \uc2 Investors in credit markets were jittery Thursday, provoking volatility in interest rate futures contracts on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange.\par \par \uc2 The contracts reflect investor expectations about annualized interest rates at future dates.\par \par \uc2 The most actively traded contract, January 2010, closed Thursday at 15.65%, down from 16.22% Tuesday. The contract rose as high as 17.72% in early trading before the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted decisively in containing the real's slide against the dollar Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 -By John Kolodziejski, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-2586-6086; john.kolodziejski@dowjones.com [ 23-10-08 1840GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081023e4an0012j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
