\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina To Expand Trade Barriers To Protect Local Industry\b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2008\par 17:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES (Dow Jones)--Faced with expectations of a widespread economic slowdown owing to the international financial crisis, Argentina is poised to step up protective barriers to shield local industry from cheap imports from China and Brazil.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Customs Director Silvina Tirabassi announced that 120 additional products would be added to a list of goods carrying a reference price fixed by the government. These prices are used by the government to designate goods that will suffer sanctions when they enter the country at a cheaper price than the reference price. When this occurs, the government alleges dumping on the part of the exporting country.\par \par \uc2 The list is mostly made up of textiles, shoes, domestic appliances, farm machinery and linens.\par \par \uc2 "In the past months we've detected fraud totaling $15 million, particularly in textiles and motorcycles," Tirabassi said, according to local daily Clarin.\par \par \uc2 While the measures aren't officially targeted at imports from any country in particular, local industrialists are worried about competition from Argentina's largest trading partner, Brazil.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has seen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunge this month in relation to the dollar, while Argentina's peso has remained relatively stable owing to \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This has made goods coming from \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  much cheaper than those produced domestically.\par \par \uc2 Brazil and Argentina are members of regional trading block Mercosur, which also includes Paraguay and Uruguay with Venezuela in the process of becoming a full member.\par \par \uc2 -By Shane Romig, Dow Jones Newswires; 54-11-4590-2438; shane.romig@dowjones.com [ 17-10-08 1535GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081017e4ah0010o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
