\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks, real plunge on global economy fears\b0\par\par\uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2008\par 20:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to mid-afternoon)\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Oct 15 (Reuters) - Brazilian shares plummeted more than 10 percent on Wednesday, triggering a trading halt, as mounting fears of global recession due to the financial crisis battered markets worldwide.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real <BRBY>, also skidded 4.53 percent lower to 2.19 per dollar from 2.095 on Tuesday, despite $1 billion in dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark stock index crumbled after notching a 17 percent gain the two previous sessions, with heavyweights \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  and Vale posting big losses along with major banks.\par \par \uc2 The Bovespa index <.BVSP> of the Sao Paulo stock exchange slumped to 37,412.54 in afternoon trade, prompting an automatic 30-minute trading halt, after ending Tuesday at 41,569.03. It continued its slide after trading resumed, for a loss of 11.04 percent.\par \par \uc2 It was the fourth halt due to a 10-percent fall since the start of last week.\par \par \uc2 The exchange will remain open at least half an hour after its scheduled 5 p.m. (2000 GMT) close on Wednesday due to the late circuit breaker, officials said.\par \par \uc2 The index had risen slightly on Tuesday, a day after soaring 14.7 percent in the biggest one-day rally since 1999 on relief over U.S. and European steps to shore up their banking sectors.\par \par \uc2 Shares of state-run \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  sank 13.37 percent to 23.65 reais on Wednesday as crude prices plunged on fears that a global recession will cut energy demand.\par \par \uc2 Mining company Vale slumped 15.31 percent to 23.46 reais, taking a hit from a sharp decline in industrial metals prices.\par \par \uc2 The real slumped even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a total of $1 billion in dollar repurchase agreements in two auctions in a bid to provide the market with added liquidity.\par \par \uc2 The bank will buy back the dollars at a fixed price 90 days after the settlement date, meaning it will temporarily add reserves to the banking system.\par \par \uc2 Selling dollars from its international reserves and repurchase agreements are just some of the ways the bank has sought to supply liquidity to the market in recent weeks. It has also sold \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps and eased bank reserve requirements several times to free up money for lending.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar is closely following stock markets abroad -- any worsening there prompts it to rise here," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 U.S. stocks <.DJI> were down nearly 6 percent as investors worried that efforts to ease the credit crisis would not be enough to avert a recession and a slump in company earnings.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian banking stocks slid. Banco Bradesco was down 9.97 percent at 25.55 reais, while Itau dropped 10.61 percent to 26.2 reais and state-run \uc2 Banco do Brasil\uc2  retreated 8.56 percent to 16.45 reais.\par \par \uc2 One of the few gainers -- albeit briefly -- was discount retailer Lojas Runner after it said it had canceled a shareholder meeting scheduled to discuss its possible takeover of rival Leader.\par \par \uc2 Investors initially pushed its shares up 0.8 percent to 20.16 reais, viewing the proposed pre-crisis price for the deal as unrealistically high. Renner shares later dropped 5.35 percent to 18.93 reais.\par \par \uc2 "Unless we see a major market rebound in the next few days, we believe the deal will be canceled by shareholders," brokerage Ativa said in a report.\par \par \uc2 Interest-rate futures <0#DIJ:> on the BM&F commodities and futures exchange were broadly higher. (Reporting by Stuart Grudgings and Aluisio Alves; Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|ABX|BNX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081015e4af001uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
