\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Market Central Banks Turn Focus To Economic Growth\b0\par\par\uc2 By Giada Cardoletti Litner   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 816 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2008\par 00:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--As the global financial crisis engulfs the developing world from Moscow to Rio, central banks are starting to shift their monetary policy focus to slowing economic growth from the fight against inflation.\par \par \uc2 In the last few days a slew of central banks have either slowed their pace of tightening, paused it or have started to cut rates.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation-fighting credibility takes a back seat to preventing economic recession in the current environment," said Paul Biszko, an emerging markets strategist with \uc2 RBC Dominion Securities\uc2  in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 But the transition into easing monetary policy won't be easy, swift or painless.\par \par \uc2 Developing world central bankers have it tougher than their developed world brethren, whose chief focus is to reignite the engines of their stagnating economies.\par \par \uc2 Despite some slowing, the developing world continues to grow at a solid pace thanks to resilient domestic demand. Nevertheless, recession in the developed world is taking a toll on emerging market economies. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  on Monday cut its 2009 gross domestic product growth forecast for developing economies to 5.5% from 6.2%.\par \par \uc2 Controlling inflation has been the top priority for emerging market central banks in 2008. Just this summer rising inflation was a global news story with the soaring cost of food and energy becoming politically volatile issues for the developing world. It also upset developed nations as inflation ate into disposable income and depressed consumer and business confidence.\par \par \uc2 But, while in the West such concerns have subsided amid a decline in commodity prices, slowing growth and plunging stock markets, in emerging markets such events have had an undesired effect on local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The strong resurgence of the U.S. dollar in recent weeks sent domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunging sharply across emerging markets, raising fears that imported inflation will add to existing inflation already above \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  targets.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's annual inflation was hovering at 6.25% in September, above the government's target of 4.5%. Chile's stood at 9.2%, or roughly three times the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 3% plus-or-minus one percentage point target.\par \par \uc2 As the credit crisis washes onto emerging market shores, central banks are caught between a rock and a hard place. They can tighten monetary policy to prevent higher inflation becoming entrenched, or they can cut interest rates to cushion financial weakness.\par \par \uc2 With companies throughout the developing world finding it difficult to raise money and dollar-denominated bond deals not getting sold, banks are being forced to shift their priorities.\par \par \uc2 "Liquidity is broken. This is a severe situation that has gone global in scope," said Biszko. "We are going to see a broad shift across central banks prioritizing growth over inflation."\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held rates steady at 8.5% despite wide expectations of another 25-basis-point hike. Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also kept its rate unchanged at 6.5% Thursday evening after increasing the reference rate six times this year.\par \par \uc2 Echoing Wednesday's coordinated rate cut in many of the largest economies in the world, other central banks are expected to follow suit.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been hiking interest rates throughout 2008, mindful of its history of hyper-inflation, could hold the Selic steady at its next rate-setting committee meeting on Oct. 29, according to some analysts.\par \par \uc2 "I would say at this moment that (Brazil's) \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is looking at external factors," said Alex Agostini, an economist at Sao Paulo-based Austin Rating Servicos Financeiros. "The coordinated action by central banks (Wednesday) lends support to the possibility that (our) \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain interest rates unchanged at the next meeting."\par \par \uc2 But the pace and size of any monetary policy easing will be done with a view to the strength or weakness of domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mexico's and Russia's central banks dipped into their large foreign reserves this week to shore up their respective tumbling \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has also been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to boost dollar liquidity, cut reserve requirements on cash and term deposits to aid the banking system facing thinning short-term credit lines for export and business operating capital.\par \par \uc2 After a decade of solid growth on the back of a boom in commodities prices, emerging market central banks are well aware that if they don't keep inflation in check this year, it will return perhaps with greater vengeance in the future.\par \par \uc2 "The worst of the rate hikes is over," said Siobhan Morden, head of Latin American markets at ABN Amro. "The markets are easing, but the timing and the amount is uncertain given their own respective domestic cycles and the passthrough to higher inflation expectations."\par \par \uc2 -By Giada Cardoletti, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4290; giada.cardoletti@dowjones.com [ 10-10-08 2207GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081010e4aa000yi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
