\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  offers dollars in 3rd auction\b0\par\par\uc2 144 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2008\par 21:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Oct 10 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will offer dollars on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for a third time on Friday.\par \par \uc2  The bank earlier offered dollars on the spot market at rates of 2.275 and 2.311 reais per dollar. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real <BRBY>, was trading 5.2 percent weaker at 2.326 per dollar shortly after the auction announcement.\par \par \uc2  The bank offered dollars in the spot market in three auctions on Wednesday and in two auctions on Thursday, dipping into international reserves for the first time since March 2003 in a bid to quench surging demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  (Reporting by Jenifer Correa, Writing by Todd Benson; Editing by Leslie Adler)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081010e4aa00204\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
