\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's real sinks to 2-year low, stocks tumble\b0\par\par\uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2008\par 17:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Oct 10 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank to its weakest level in more than two years on Friday even as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  flooded the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with dollars, while stocks dropped for a seventh session as investors fled emerging market securities.\par \par \uc2 The Bovespa index <.BVSP> of the Sao Paulo stock exchange sank rapidly from the start of trade to rack up losses of 10 percent, triggering an automatic 30-minute halt to trading.\par \par \uc2 After resuming trade, the index clawed back in a volatile session to end 3.97 percent lower at 35,609.54 points, its lowest close since September 2006.\par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> plunged 5.3 percent to 2.326 per U.S. dollar, its weakest close since May 2006, despite three \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. It was the third time the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this week to help prop up the real.\par \par \uc2 The bank also sold $589 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, which work like the sale of dollars in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 With Friday's losses, the real has now shed more than a third of its value since Aug. 1, when it hit a nine-year high.\par \par \uc2 "The market is looking very bad," said Luis Piason, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at the Concordia brokerage. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it didn't have much of an impact."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sought to reassure investors on Friday, saying it has no limit as a lender of last resort to the local banking system and that its main objective was for local markets to function properly.\par \par \uc2 Over just the last four months, the Bovespa has given up all its gains made in a long rally since the start of 2006 that took it to a high of 73,920 at the end of May.\par \par \uc2 Traders said Friday's fall was on concerns that plummeting global markets will cut capital flows to developing countries and on fears that the worst may not be over for U.S. stocks.\par \par \uc2 Energy giant \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  , the top-weighted stock in the index, dropped 7.26 percent to 24.00 reais, as oil prices fell below $80 a barrel for the first time in a year.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian airlines were hammered by fears of slumping demand for air travel in the expected economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 Gol Linhas Aereas\uc2  fell 1.14 percent to 8.66 reais, while \uc2 TAM Linhas Aereas\uc2  , Brazil's leading airline, slumped 4.2 percent to 26.44 reais.\par \par \uc2 Gol Chief Executive Constantino de Oliveira Junior told Reuters in an interview late on Thursday that the company is bracing for a potential slowdown in air travel stemming from the financial crisis by bringing its loss-making Varig unit under the same roof to standardize services and cut costs.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian real estate developers sank on expectations a global slowdown and steep credit crunch will reduce financing for mortgages. Gafisa , Brazil's largest developer, sank 14.2 percent to 12.90 reais, while Cyrela fell 4.55 percent to 10.90 reais. (Reporting by Fabio Gehrke and Elzio Barreto; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081010e4aa001pi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
