\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's real posts biggest loss since Jan. 2002\b0\par\par\uc2 180 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2008\par 21:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Oct 6 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted its biggest one-day loss on Monday in more than six years, plunging 7 percent as a deepening global financial crisis battered markets around the world.\par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> slumped to 2.20 per U.S. dollar from 2.046 on Friday, closing at its lowest level since Sept. 26, 2006. It was the real's biggest one-day loss since Jan. 8, 2002, when it tumbled almost 11 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the session in a bid to quench surging demand for dollars, offering dollar swaps for the first time in more than two years. It sold $1.47 billion in swaps of $2.1 billion on offer in an auction.\par \par \uc2 With Monday's losses, the real has now weakened 19.2 percent so far this year, nearly wiping out a 20 percent surge in 2007.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Fabio Gehrke, Writing by Todd Benson)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL/REAL (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081006e4a6001r0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
