\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weaker Early On Commodities Decline, Dollar Climb\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2008\par 15:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real weakened in early trading Tuesday as investors reacted cautiously to continued declines in key commodities prices and the climb of the dollar against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid international uncertainties.\par \par \uc2 As of 1350 GMT, the real was trading at BRL1.6545 per dollar after ending at BRL1.6460 on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange Monday.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the real continued to slide as investors unwound defensive positions in oil, metals and grains markets with Hurricane Gustav, now a tropical depression, passing through the Gulf of Mexico causing less damage than had been feared.\par \par \uc2 Investors, meanwhile, were closely monitoring the dollar's continued climb against the euro, after adverse economic data in recent sessions cast doubts over the trajectory of the Euro zone economy.\par \par \uc2 The market Tuesday was also closely watching Asia, where a political crisis in Thailand prompted at least five banks in the region to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Locally, meanwhile, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's IBGE statistics institute reported that industrial production continued at a strong pace in July, rising by 1% from the previous month and by 8.5% compared with the same month a year earlier. The figures came in at the high end of market estimates, and according to analysts, could prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain its current tight monetary policy stance at upcoming interest rate meetings. The bank has raised the country's reference Selic rate by 1.75 percentage points so far this year to 13% annually in an effort to curb inflation pressure.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, is seen maintaining some pressure on the real later in the session Tuesday with a customary daily dollar auction.\par \par \uc2 The bank has purchased dollars in daily auctions since late 2005 in an effort to boost foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 As of the latest available figures Monday, reserves stand at $205.12 billion.\par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832, gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 02-09-08 1306GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080902e492000lh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
