\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Closes Stronger On Recovering Commodities   \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 20:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real rebounded Tuesday as commodities prices recovered overseas.   \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended trading at BRL1.731 per dollar per dollar spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F, stronger than Monday's close of BRL1.746.   \par \par \uc2 The recovery of commodities prices overseas brought money back into Brazil's raw material heavy assets.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, short-term investment inflows were boosted Tuesday by rising expectations of a hike in local interest rates amid concerns over creeping inflation. According to a market survey released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, expectations for IPCA consumer price inflation over the coming 12 months rose to 4.33% from 4.29% seen previously.   \par \par \uc2 The threat that Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be forced to raise the country's reference Selic interest rate from its current level of 11.25% annually has heightened investor interest in local government securities.   \par \par \uc2 The real was undermined by the news that Sao Paulo state canceled the privatization auction of electric utility  \uc2 Companhia Energetica de Sao Paulo SA\uc2  (CESP5.BR), or Cesp, due to take place Wednesday, because of a lack of interest from potential bidders.   \par \par \uc2 Investors had expected heavy inflows following the sale of the asset, which was priced in excess of BRL6.6 billion.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chose to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday, after staying on the sidelines Monday.   \par \par \uc2 The bank has purchased dollars in daily auctions since late 2005 in an effort to boost foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in local rate futures trading, rates rose amid strengthening ideas that an interest rate hike is around the corner.   \par \par \uc2 The rate on the most heavily traded contract, January 2010, ended at 13.23%, up from 13.20% on Monday. Brazil's interbank overnight rate was flat at 11.10%.   \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart; Dow Jones Newswires; 5511 3145-1479; alastair.stewart@dowjones.com [ 25-03-08 1927GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080325e43p000zt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
