\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks rise on joint bank moves, real dips   \b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2007\par 17:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Dec 12 (Reuters) - Brazil's stock market ended higher on Wednesday after the U.S. Federal Reserve joined with other central banks to ease tight conditions in global credit markets, but the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened in volatile trading.   \par \par \uc2 The Bovespa index <.BVSP> of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange finished 0.36 percent higher at 64,741.69 points after rising more than 1 percent earlier in the session, snapping three days of losses that pushed the index down nearly 2 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> initially rose in tandem with the stock market, but reversed course late in the session and finished almost 1 percent weaker at 1.774 per U.S. dollar. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars late in the day, helping to push the real lower.   \par \par \uc2 The Fed said on Wednesday it would launch a temporary short-term lending facility that banks can use at its discount window, a move that was coordinated with similar moves by the Bank of England, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other major central banks.   \par \par \uc2 The initiative revived some of the appetite for riskier emerging market assets, which has sagged recently. It also came after the Fed's decision on Tuesday to cut its benchmark lending rate by 25 basis points, which disappointed some investors.   \par \par \uc2 "This move by the central banks will help calm down the markets. It is as if with this announcement to add liquidity, they're saying they're not going to let anyone go broke," said Hamilton Moreira, a senior investment analyst at BB Investimentos.   \par \par \uc2 Interest-rate futures <0#DIJ:> on the Brazilian commodities and futures bourse BM&F were mixed even after the Fed move helped improve investor sentiment.   \par \par \uc2 At the stock market, shares of state-controlled oil company  \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  , the heaviest-weighted stock in the Bovespa index, jumped 5.06 percent to 84.99 reais as oil prices soared in New York and London.   \par \par \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  also said it had cranked up a huge 180,000-barrel-per-day rig after many delays, finally meeting this year's capacity growth target.   \par \par \uc2 Retailer CBD rose 3.53 percent to 35.20 reais after the company late on Tuesday named named Claudio Galeazzi, an executive known for turning around struggling companies, as its new chief executive. CBD on Monday fired Cassio Casseb, who was CEO for nearly two years. (Reporting by Rodolfo Barbosa and Todd Benson; editing by Gary Crosse)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|M|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071212e3cc001c1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
