\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Fin Min: New Fund Will Counter Real's Appreciation -FT   \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2007\par 00:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \uc2 Brazilian Finance Minister Guido Mantega said the nation will create a sovereign wealth fund with the primary aim of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to counter the appreciation of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , The Financial Times reported Sunday on its Web site.   \par \par \uc2 Since the fund was announced by Mantega in October, funding plans and objectives have undergone several revisions, the FT reported.   \par \par \uc2 According to the FT, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said, "The big victory for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that the fund will have nothing to do with Brazil's foreign reserves and nothing to do with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2 But in an interview with the FT in Brasilia, Mantega said the fund would indeed affect the accumulation of reserves and would share the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's source of funding at the national treasury. Under current rules, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is the sole prerogative of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "It will have the function of reducing the offer of dollars in the market and helping the real to appreciate less," Mantega told the FT.   \par \par \uc2 Under Mantega's original plan, the sovereign wealth fund would have drawn on Brazil's foreign reserves, which have risen quickly this year to about $180 billion. That plan sparked a behind-the-scenes row between the Finance Ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the FT said.   \par \par \uc2 Newspaper Web site:   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.ft.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.ft.com  }}}\uc2  [ 09-12-07 2339GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071209e3c900097\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
