\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weakens Slightly From 7-Yr High In Light Trade   \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2007\par 15:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Gerald Jeffris   \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real was slightly weaker against the dollar in early trading Monday, falling away from a seven-year high amid reduced foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows brought about by the closure of some U.S. markets for the Columbus Day holiday.   \par \par \uc2 As of 1340 GMT, the real was trading at BRL1.807 per dollar after ending at BRL1.803 per dollar Friday in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange.   \par \par \uc2 Traders noted participants would likely take profits while waiting for further data due out during the week on the strength of the international economy.   \par \par \uc2 "The real will likely depreciate a bit today as market players tend to be cautious in relation to indicators due out this week," said trader at a Sao Paulo-based brokerage.   \par \par \uc2 In particular, analysts said the market would be looking to the minutes of the U.S. Federal Reserve's September monetary policy meeting for hints about whether that \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to cut interest rates at upcoming rate meetings.   \par \par \uc2 Locally, meanwhile, economic forecasts remained mostly tame, with projections for IPCA consumer price inflation holding practically unchanged in a weekly \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  market survey.   \par \par \uc2 According to the survey, the forecast for the year-end 2007 ICPA moved up a tick to 4.01% from 4.00% seen the previous week. The projection for 2008 IPCA inflation held steady at 4.10%.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's government has set year-end inflation targets of 4.5% for both years.   \par \par \uc2 Investors remained in doubt meanwhile about whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through daily dollar purchase auctions.   \par \par \uc2 The bank suspended auctions in August after having purchased more than $75 billion in the first seven months of the year to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Some analysts, however, have warned that the bank may resume auctions if the real rises firmly above the BRL1.80 per dollar market.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, according to the bank's latest market survey, the real is seen ending October at BRL1.85 per dollar and also finishing 2007 at the same level.   \par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 3335-0832; gerald.jeffrisdowjones.com [ 08-10-07 1347GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071008e3a8000w8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
