\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks surge to record, real up on Fed hope   \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2007\par 15:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Sept 26 (Reuters) - Brazil's stock market rose to a record high on Wednesday and the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained on growing expectations the U.S. Federal Reserve would cut interest rates in October, raising the appeal of emerging market securities.   \par \par \uc2 The Bovespa index <.BVSP> of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange jumped 1.39 percent to 59,676.4 points, closing at a record high for a third straight session. The index surged about 34 percent so far in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real <BRBY>, strengthened 0.75 percent to 1.847 per U.S. dollar rising for the second session.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed near its strongest level since 2000, taking cues from strong gains in the Bovespa index and equity markets in the United States and Europe.   \par \par \uc2 Expectations the Fed may cut interest rates again next month sent Brazilian assets higher as lower U.S. rates generally fuel the appetite for high-yield, riskier emerging market securities.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in more than a month and isn't likely to step in even as investment inflows surge, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to register a very strong flow to resume buying dollars," said Jorge Knauer, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Banco Proper in Rio de Janeiro.   \par \par \uc2 Interest rate futures <0#DIJ:> on the BM&F futures exchange in Sao Paulo were mostly down, reflecting the positive investor sentiment and gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets.   \par \par \uc2 On the stock market, shares of iron ore miner CVRD , the second-heaviest stock in the index, was up 1.76 percent to 50.8 reais even as nickel and copper prices eased in international markets.   \par \par \uc2 State-controlled oil company  \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  , the top-weighted stock in the index, gained 1.25 percent to 59.85 reais. The company said on Wednesday it will raise the price of aviation fuel by 4.5 percent starting on Oct. 1 because of higher international oil prices.  \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  has no plans to raise prices of gasoline and diesel, said Paulo Roberto Costa, the company's downstream director.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070926e39q0014c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
