\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's cenbank holds 2nd auction to buy dollars   \b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2007\par 20:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, July 13 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold its second auction of the day on Friday to buy U.S. dollars on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as part of an effort to build up international reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real <BRBY>, was 0.43 percent stronger at 1.866 per dollar shortly after the announcement. The real has traded below 2.0 per dollar since May 15, when it broke that level for the first time in six years.   \par \par \uc2 It was the first time since May 4 that the bank held two auctions in one day.   \par \par \uc2 The bank has aggressively bought dollars over the past year to increase reserves and, indirectly, blunt the real's gains. It has bought nearly $57 billion on the spot market in 2007, surpassing the $35.1 billion it bought in all of 2006. (Reporting by Silvio Cascione)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070713e37d001rr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
