\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil's Real Opens Weaker On China Tax Decision   \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2007\par 14:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, May 30, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real opened slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday after China announced a hike in taxes on stock market transactions.   \par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL1.963 per dollar, slightly weaker against the Tuesday close of BRL1.949.   \par \par \uc2 Earlier Tuesday, the Chinese government announced a rise in taxes on stock market transactions. According to analysts, the move could hurt investments in all emerging market countries.   \par \par \uc2 The market also turned cautious in Brazil Wednesday ahead of release of minutes from the most recent U.S. Federal Reserve Board meeting. At the meeting, the board held the U.S. base rate steady at 5.25%.   \par \par \uc2 Investors in Brazil will be looking for signs as to future Fed moves. The expectation is that the minutes will show an increasingly cautious Fed, diminishing chances for an interest rate cut in the U.S. this year.   \par \par \uc2 Wednesday's Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will also be marked by the monthly battle over the so-called Ptax rate. The Ptax, or average \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, for Thursday will be used to settle \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures contracts. Jockeying to influence the rate typically begins a day or two before the settlement, which is always the last working day of the month.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could also decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market later Wednesday. The bank often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , usually as a buyer of dollars. Heavy buying by the bank could weaken the real even more, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 -By Tom Murphy, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1478; brazil@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 05-30-07 0836ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070530e35u001xf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
