\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil's Real Ends Stronger Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Dlr Buying   \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2007\par 21:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 May 28, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Despite a late-afternoon market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real ended stronger against the dollar Monday for the second consecutive session amid continued firm inflows from trade and investment to local markets.   \par \par \uc2 The real ended at BRL1.9425 per dollar after ending BRL1.9510 in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange Friday.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  got support during the session from steady flows of incoming foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid continued improvements in local economic forecasts.   \par \par \uc2 According to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey released Monday, Brazil's IPCA consumer price inflation was seen falling by the end of this year to 3.5% from 3.6% seen previously. Brazil's government has set a year-end inflation target of 4.5%.   \par \par \uc2 At the same time, the survey showed that economic growth in 2007 would rise to 4.16% from 4.10% seen earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Alongside the effects of favorable economic forecasts, the real also took strength during the session from continued firm trade inflows.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's trade ministry early Monday reported Brazil saw a $700 million foreign trade surplus in the May 21-27 period, which brought the country's surplus for the year to date to $16.39 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Continued strong inflows from trade and investment sources prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy an unspecified quantified dollars at an auction late in the session at a rate of BRL1.9445.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was insufficient to suppress the strength of the real, however, and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to gain steam through the end of the session.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in local interest rate markets Monday, the rate on the most actively traded futures contract, January 2010, fell to 10.31% from 10.33% at Friday's close. Brazil's interbank overnight rate rose, however, to 12.36% from 12.35%.   \par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 4501-7143; gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 05-28-07 1550ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070528e35s001hb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
