\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil's Meirelles: Pace Of Interest Rate Easing Adequate   \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2007\par 19:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, May 24, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 The pace of interest rate easing in Brazil has been adequate and shouldn't be altered solely in reaction to recent exchange rate appreciation, Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique Meirelles said Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 "The fact is that interest rates are falling," he said. "Some people might believe that the trajectory of their decline is timid and others might even believe that it is too fast, but we believe that it is adequate to maintain inflation within targets and country risk in decline."   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut the country's reference Selic interest rate by 7.25 percentage points since September 2005 to a current 12.5% annually.   \par \par \uc2 Speaking at a joint hearing before six congressional committees on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities, Meirelles denied that the real's appreciation was prompted by speculative foreign investment in high Brazilian interest rates and said it was mostly influenced by robust foreign trade surpluses and a weakening of the U.S. dollar internationally.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's real has strengthened about 9% against the dollar since the beginning of the year.   \par \par \uc2 Some analysts have suggested that Brazil should accelerate interest rate cuts to diminish strong flows of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the country.   \par \par \uc2 According to data presented by Meirelles, despite the real's appreciation against the dollar it has remained mostly stable against a group of at least 15 other world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  examined by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Meirelles Thursday reiterated past declarations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no intention to set a target for the exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2 "Brazil has already used a target for the exchange rate, but that had to be abandoned during a crisis in 1998," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Despite Meirelles' declarations, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with dollar purchase auctions almost daily since 2005. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to diminish market volatility and build the country's foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Meirelles, meanwhile, said he believed the country's interest rates would continue to decline amid low inflation expectations.   \par \par \uc2 According to recent market surveys, Brazil's IPCA consumer price inflation is seen ending 2007 and 2008 at below the country's official target of 4.5%.   \par \par \uc2 Meirelles noted that Brazil's real interest rate is currently around 7.5% annually, a level well below highs of around 22% seen in the previous 10 years.   \par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 4501-7143, geraldjeffrisdowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 05-24-07 1336ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070524e35o004ia\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
