\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil's Real Opens Slightly Weaker As Recent Surge Eases   \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2007\par 15:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 May 17, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 By Jeff Fick   \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real opened slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar Thursday, falling back from a six-year high as a recent surge in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased.   \par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL1.955 per dollar in trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, weaker from Wednesday's close of BRL1.953. That was the highest close for the real since January 2001.   \par \par \uc2 According to traders, Thursday's session was likely to see investors locking in profits from the real's recent surge. However, the overall trend for the real continues to be stronger, given the country's solid economic fundamentals that have attracted heavy investment inflows.   \par \par \uc2 In addition, credit-ratings agency  \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  on Wednesday upgraded its long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign credit rating on the country to BB+, one notch below investment grade, from BB. The move further boosted positive sentiment toward investments in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 However, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in an effort to smooth out the real's appreciation. After sitting on the sidelines as the real broke the 2-to-1 barrier on Tuesday, the bank purchased about $2 billion in reverse-swap and spot market snap auctions on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the risk to investing in Brazil as measured by the  \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus, or EMBI+, tightened to a spread of 144 basis points over U.S. Treasurys. Brazil's benchmark Global 40 bond was flat at a bid of 135 3/4.   \par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1481; jeff.fick@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 05-17-07 0914ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070517e35h0018b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
