\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves help lower risk premium-c.bank   \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2007\par 19:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, May 9 (Reuters) - The lower risk now attached to holding Brazilian assets cushions the cost from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to steady its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently aggressively bought lower-yielding dollars to weaken the real <BRL=>, which is hovering at 6 1/2 year highs.   \par \par \uc2 "There is no doubt there is a cost of carrying the reserves or carrying a long position in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Henrique Meirelles, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president told a news conference in London.   \par \par \uc2 "But that basically also generates a saving, which is the lower perceived risk for the country. The risk for the balance of payments decreases and that is reflected in the decrease of the risk premium on Brazilian paper."   \par \par \uc2 The spread between Brazilian debt and U.S. Treasuries on the  \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  EMBI+ index <11EMJ> is currently around 155 basis points near a recent record tight level of 146 basis points.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's international reserves have been rising rapidly and Meirelles said they were currently around $120 billion, the bulk of which is held in U.S.-denominated assets.   \par \par \uc2 He was upbeat on Brazil's economic fundamentals and asked whether he was worried inflation was reaching too low a level he said: "We are well within the target zone. The inflation targeting regime is working properly."   \par \par \uc2 He said the target zone for Brazilian inflation was between 2.5 and 6.5 percent with a mid point at 4.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 With annual inflation running at about 3 percent, the bank has come under pressure from some business leaders and politicians to relax monetary policy and cut interest rates faster to give the economy a boost.   \par \par \uc2 But Meirelles said over the weekend the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not ease up in the battle against inflation, even though consumer prices are rising at the slowest pace in years.   \par \par \uc2 He declined to comment on monetary policy.   \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-BRAZIL-MEIRELLES/|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070509e359001xj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
