\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil Real Weaker Early As Mkt Mulls US Data, Brazil Ctrl Bk   \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2007\par 15:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 May 04, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 Gerald Jeffris   \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real weakened slightly against the dollar in early trading Friday as investors maintained a cautious stance awaiting reaction to just-released U.S. payroll data and possible continued strong market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 As of 1240 GMT, the real was at BRL2.028 per dollar per dollar after ending at BRL2.027 in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the market was in a holding pattern as investors evaluated whether payrolls confirmed an alteration in the pace of the U.S. economy.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Labor Department reported at 1230 GMT that job growth in April was at its slowest pace since November 2004.   \par \par \uc2 Investors were also keeping a close eye on continued moves by Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the dollar locally.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market with unexpectedly heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, selling $3 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts after the real threatened to surge upward of BRL2.00 per dollar in midsession action.   \par \par \uc2 In the previous sessions it had sold only between $400 million and $600 million in swaps daily. The swap auctions allow investors to exchange paper linked to variations in the Brazilian real against the U.S. dollar for government paper linked to interest rates. The swaps, which permit foreign investors to enjoy Brazil's high domestic interest rates without \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure, typically help weaken the real by reducing future dollar inflows.   \par \par \uc2 Alongside the swap auction, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market with a spot dollar purchase auction Thursday, buying an unspecified quantity of dollars at BRL2.027.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been purchasing dollars at daily auctions since 2005 in an effort to build up foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 As of Wednesday, reserves stood at $122.4 billion.   \par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 4501-7143, gerald.jeffrisdowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 05-04-07 0903ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070504e354001ck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
