\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Closes Weaker On Heavy  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2007\par 21:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, May 03, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 By Jeff Fick   \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Thursday on heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after inflows pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a fresh six-year high early in the session.   \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.027 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F, weaker from Wednesday's close of BRL2.023 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  undermined the real, which reached a six-year high of BRL2.008 per dollar early in the session. Heavy inflows from foreign investors and sales of exporter dollars pushed the real to the brink of BRL2.0 per dollar, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  then announced a surprise auction of the equivalent of $3 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts, the largest such auction ever held by the bank.   \par \par \uc2 The bank offered 63,050 contracts covering four different maturities between November 2007 and July 2009. The contracts offer investors the opportunity to swap dollar-linked paper for bonds tied to domestic interest rates.   \par \par \uc2 Such auctions typically help to strengthen the U.S. dollar against the Brazilian real because they reduce pressure from future dollar inflows.   \par \par \uc2 Thursday's auction followed a similar auction Wednesday of the equivalent of $600 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps.   \par \par \uc2 Immediately after the bank called the auction, the real weakened to BRL2.022 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 In addition, the bank held a snap auction on the spot market, buying an undisclosed volume of dollars late in the session. The bank said it's purchasing dollars to build up foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The bank bought dollars for BRL2.027 per dollar. In the minutes before the auction, the real traded at BRL2.024 per dollar. Moments after the auction, the real was trading at BRL2.027 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have flooded Brazil with cash amid a bull run on the Brazilian Stock Exchange, or Bovespa. In addition, Brazil's Selic base interest rate currently stands at 12.5%, one of the highest rates in the world despite 15-consecutive rate cuts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 While real interest rates remain high, they are trending downward on expectations for more aggressive rate cuts by the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at future meetings.   \par \par \uc2 Local interest rate futures declined Thursday, matching a fall at the Brazilian Treasury's latest bond auction held earlier in the day. The most actively traded local interest rate futures contract, July 2007, closed at 12.19%, down from Wednesday's close at 12.20%.   \par \par \uc2 The contracts project probable annualized interest charges for the overnight interbank rate at future dates.   \par \par \uc2 The actual overnight interbank rate for Thursday was 12.34%, flat with Wednesday's close.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the risk to investing in Brazil as measured by the  \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  Emerging Market Bond Index Plus tightened slightly to a spread of 152 basis points over U.S. Treasurys as of 1912 GMT. The benchmark Brazil 2040 bond was down 3/16 at 135 13/16 bid.   \par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1481; jeff.fick@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 05-03-07 1521ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070503e3530047r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
