\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Weaker Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2007\par 21:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Apr 27, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Friday under the weight of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The real ended at BRL2.031 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F, weaker from Thursday's close of BRL2.027 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its recent intense activity on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Friday. It sold the equivalent of $600 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts and it also held a snap auction on the spot market, buying an undisclosed volume of dollars late in the session.   \par \par \uc2 According to traders, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be trying to take a stand to prevent the exchange rate from going under two to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps offer investors the opportunity to swap bonds linked to the U.S. dollar for paper indexed to domestic interest rates. The auctions often help strengthen the dollar by reducing future dollar inflows.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real was offered support by weak U.S. growth data, causing investors to weigh the possibility of monetary policy loosening there.   \par \par \uc2 Earlier Friday, the U.S. Commerce Department released data showing that the U.S. economy slowed sharply in early 2007, retreating to its weakest pace in four years. Gross domestic product rose at a seasonally adjusted 1.3% annual rate January through March, lower than a forecast 1.8%.   \par \par \uc2 Investors were still digesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's minutes from its April meeting, released Thursday, which indicated that bankers felt rising imports were offsetting inflationary pressures caused by domestic demand.   \par \par \uc2 Economists are keenly debating whether the bank will make a 50-basis-point cut at the next meeting on June 6.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's Selic base rate currently stands at 12.5% after 15 consecutive rate cuts.   \par \par \uc2 The most actively traded local interest rate futures contract, January 2009, closed at 11.07%, up from Thursday's close at 10.98%.   \par \par \uc2 The contracts project probable annualized interest charges for the overnight interbank rate at future dates.   \par \par \uc2 The actual overnight interbank rate for Friday was 12.35%, down from 12.36% at Thursday's close.   \par \par \uc2 The risk to investing in Brazil as measured by the  \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  Emerging Market Bond Index Plus loosened to a spread of 149 basis points over U.S. Treasurys as of 1903 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511 3145-1479; alastair.stewart@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 04-27-07 1529ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070427e34r002pf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
