\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Weaker On Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Prospect   \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2007\par 14:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 Apr 27, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 By Alastair Stewart   \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real opened weaker against the U.S. dollar Friday amid the prospect of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL2.034 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F, weaker from Thursday's close of BRL2.027 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up its activity on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the past couple of days. It sold the equivalent of $600 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts on Thursday and it also held a snap auction on the spot market, buying an undisclosed volume of dollars late in the session.   \par \par \uc2 According to traders, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be taking a stand to try to prevent the exchange rate going under two to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 But with heavy dollar inflows from exports, foreign direct investment, stock market investment and foreign debt issues, the real is not seen likely to cede much ground, they added.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps offer investors the opportunity to swap bonds linked to the U.S. dollar for paper indexed to domestic interest rates. The auctions often help strengthen the dollar by reducing future dollar inflows.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real will find support from data showing U.S. economy slowed sharply in early 2007, retreating to its weakest pace in four years. Gross domestic product rose at a seasonally adjusted 1.3% annual rate January through March, lower than a forecast 1.8%.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the market continues to digest the minutes from the Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's April meeting, which raised expectations for a more aggressive pace of interest rate cuts. Market watchers expect the bank to reduce the benchmark Selic rate by 50 basis points when it next meets June 6.   \par \par \uc2 The Selic base rate currently stands at 12.5% after 15 consecutive rate cuts.   \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511 3145-1479; alastair.stewart@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 04-27-07 0857ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070427e34r001ho\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
