\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Stronger As Ctrl Bk Doesn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bernd Radowitz   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2007\par 21:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real closed slightly stronger Tuesday on the absence of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reverse swap auction.   \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.0345 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, from BRL2.036 per dollar at Monday's close.   \par \par \uc2 The real had been weakening through much of Tuesday's session, but began to strengthen in the afternoon as Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday abstained from holding another surprise snap auction of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps.   \par \par \uc2 The swap auctions allow investors to exchange paper linked to variations in the Brazilian real against the U.S. dollar for government paper linked to interest rates. The swaps, which permit foreign investors to enjoy Brazil's high domestic interest rates without \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure, typically help weaken the real by reducing future dollar inflows.   \par \par \uc2 The bank last week adopted a new rule that allows it to call such auctions with little or no prior notice. Previously, such auctions were rare and were always scheduled following close consultations between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and brokers.   \par \par \uc2 The bank in the late afternoon bought an undisclosed amount of dollars in a common spot market auction, but the auction didn't alter the exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weaken strengthened early in the trading session, a trend intensified by the release of disappointing economic data in the U.S.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. consumer confidence fell significantly in April, with a reverse in consumer optimism about present conditions leading the decline, according to a report released Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The Conference Board, a private research group, said its index of consumer confidence for April moved to 104.0 compared with the upwardly revised 108.2 seen in March. It was the second monthly decline in a row.   \par \par \uc2 Sales of existing homes in the U.S., meanwhile, plunged in March by the largest amount in nearly two decades, reflecting bad weather and increasing problems in the subprime mortgage market, a real estate trade group reported Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The National Association of Realtors reported that sales of existing homes fell by 8.4% in March, compared to February.   \par \par \uc2 -By Bernd Radowitz, Dow Jones Newswires; +5521-3288-5004; bernd.radowitz@dowjones.com [ 24-04-07 1926GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070424e34o0014v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
