\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  edge lower in early trade  \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2007\par 16:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, March 27 (Reuters) - Brazil's stocks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged down in slow trade on Tuesday as the domestic economy supported potential gains but traders took cues from markets in the United States.  \par \par \uc2 The Bovespa index <.BVSP> of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange fell 0.41 percent to 45,459 points. The Brazilian real <BRBY> weakened 0.15 percent to 2.064 per U.S. dollar before a likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is carefully watching foreign markets," said Julio Cesar Vogeler, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the Didier Levy brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 High interest rates, currently at 12.75 percent, and sound economic fundamentals have lured foreign investors to Latin America's largest country, though worries about the health of the U.S. economy have checked local gains.  \par \par \uc2 At the stock market, bellwether and oil driller Petrobras was off 0.45 percent at 44.40 reais.  \par \par \uc2 Beverage company AmBev fell 0.93 percent to 1,222.50 reais. A newspaper report said the unit of InBev could buy the Cintra brewery in Rio de Janeiro state for about $150 million. AmBev officials declined comment.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070327e33r001bj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
