\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Brazil's Real Stronger Early As Market Tracks Inflows  \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2007\par 14:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Feb 26, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 Gerald Jeffris  \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--Brazil's real strengthened against the dollar in early trading Monday as the market saw robust inflows from recent overseas financing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and continued strong foreign trade.  \par \par \uc2 As of 1310 GMT, the real was at BRL2.084 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange after ending at BRL2.091 per dollar Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the trend for the real continued to be on an upward path regardless of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to curb the strength of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with daily dollar purchase auctions.  \par \par \uc2 "The real will likely continue to gain against the dollar, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the still very positive international outlook for \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," noted a Sao Paulo-based trader.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up dollar purchases in the market over recent weeks after the real threatened to push through BRL2.00 per dollar and spoil Brazil's foreign trade strength.  \par \par \uc2 The bank said it bought $4.8 billion in the market in January, its highest monthly amount on record, and some market observers are projecting purchases of up to $6 billion in February.  \par \par \uc2 Traders, however, noted that greenbacks continue to flow into Brazil through both financial and trade \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Among the latest of those was a $250 million overseas financing deal obtained by a local pulp and paper producer.  \par \par \uc2 Local economic factors, meanwhile, appear to favor the consolidation of the real's strength.  \par \par \uc2 In a weekly market survey released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, economists projected a slight decline in Brazil's IPCA consumer price inflation for 2007 to 3.91% from 3.94% seen previously. The market projection for Brazil's reference Selic interest rate remained stable at 11.50%.  \par \par \uc2 End-March projections for the real fell slightly, to BRL2.10 per dollar from BRL2.11 seen previously. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen weakening through the end of 2007 to BRL2.15 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 -By Gerald Jeffris, Dow Jones Newswires; (5561) 4501-7143; geraldjeffris@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 02-26-07 0823ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070226e32q001fn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
