\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Weaker Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2007\par 19:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 23, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Friday on confirmation of aggressive dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past month.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.091 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F, weaker than the BRL2.082 at the close Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost ground amid news that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought almost $7 billion during its daily spot market auctions in February thru Feb. 22.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on the local market late Friday, buying an undisclosed number of dollars at 2.092.  \par \par \uc2 "The auctions are decisive at the moment but the real still strengthens when unhindered," said Miriam Tavares at the local AGK brokerage firm in Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 According to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, net dollar inflows totaled $5.36 billion in February up to Feb. 22, with $3.05 billion coming from financial transactions and the rest from trade. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long positions rose to $5.0 billion from $3.4 billion at the end of January.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the high level of dollar inflows via the derivatives markets led players to speculate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may begin holding reverse swap auctions once again.  \par \par \uc2 Swap auctions allow investors to exchange paper linked to variations in the Brazilian real against the U.S. dollar for government paper linked to interest rates. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held regular reverse swap auctions in late 2005 and early 2006 to curb immediate dollar inflows. Since then, it has held them occasionally to rollover swap contracts.  \par \par \uc2 Domestically, the benign inflation outlook continues. Early Friday, the Getulio Vargas Foundation reported that the IPC-S inflation index registered price rises of 0.43% in the 30 days up to Feb. 22, down from 0.54% in the thirty days up to Feb. 15. The result was within the forecast range of 0.37% to 0.56%.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  next meets on March 7, when it is expected to cut the benchmark Selic base rate by as much as 50 basis points. The Selic base rate currently stands at 13.0%.  \par \par \uc2 Local interest rate futures were mixed with nearby contracts going slightly lower but longer-term futures rising amid concerns about the 2008 inflationary scenario. The most actively traded local interest rate futures contract, April 2007, closed at 12.72%, down from 12.73% on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The contracts project probable annualized interest charges for the overnight interbank rate at future dates.  \par \par \uc2 The actual overnight interbank rate for Friday was 12.89%, down from Thursday's close of 12.90%.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the risk to investing in Brazil as measured by the JP Morgan Emerging Market Bond Index Plus rose to a spread of 179 basis points over U.S. Treasurys as of 1800 GMT. The benchmark Brazil 2040 bond was flat at 133 7/8 bid.  \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart; Dow Jones Newswires; 5511 3145-1479; alastair.stewart@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 02-23-07 1327ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070223e32n00224\par }\page {\par\fs