\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  retreat after rally   \b0\par\par\uc2 451 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2007\par 15:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 23 (Reuters) - Brazil's stock market shed about 1 percent on Friday, retreating from record highs on profit-taking and after a small Wall Street decline, while the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened slightly for a second day.   \par \par \uc2 The Bovespa index <.BVSP> of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange dropped 0.94 percent to 46,015.79 points on a turnover of 2.8 billion reais ($1.3 billion), one day after setting a record close of 46,452.   \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY>, which had surged to a nine-month high earlier this week, finished 0.34 percent weaker than Thursday's close, at 2.09 per U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "It was much more of a profit-taking when you are looking for reasons than some real motive provoking profit-taking," said Marcelo Voss, chief economist with Liquidez brokerage.   \par \par \uc2 He said that after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to rise above the 2.05 mark this week despite a strong rally, many players took dollar-buying positions. Also, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's regular dollar-buying auction pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower on Friday.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in recent months to buy dollars as part of an ongoing effort to build up international reserves, which are at a record high.   \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have done little to rein in the hard-charging real, whose rally is worrying exporters and business leaders. They fear the strong exchange rate is making Brazilian products less competitive on world markets.   \par \par \uc2 In the stock market, shares in mining firm  \uc2 Cia Vale do Rio Doce\uc2  -- the world's largest producer and exporter of iron ore -- fell 1.57 percent to 65 reais.   \par \par \uc2 "The market had hit record highs so now people are grabbing the opportunity to pocket the profits ... especially in Vale, which had risen a lot," said Rodrigo Mattos, a trader with Agenda brokerage.   \par \par \uc2 Bovespa's top heavyweight, state-run oil giant Petrobras , climbed 0.84 percent to 45.43 reais as oil prices rose above $61 per barrel in New York.   \par \par \uc2 Brazilian markets have rallied of late as foreign investors pour cash into high-yielding assets in emerging markets.   \par \par \uc2 Brazil's low inflation rate, rising international reserves, wide trade surplus and high benchmark interest rate of 13 percent are attracting large inflows of dollars.   \par \par \uc2 On Friday Brazil said it posted a current account surplus of $325 million for January, compared with a $308 million deficit a year earlier and forecasts of a $225 million deficit. The numbers underscored Brazil's improving public finances.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|U|M|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070223e32n00191\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
