\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Stable Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2007\par 12:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 23, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real opened stable against the U.S. dollar Friday amid aggressive dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past couple of days.  \par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL2.082 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F.  \par \par \uc2 With no key indicators or speeches expected Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will focus on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 "The sales have stopped the real strengthening, but not caused it to move in the other direction," said Miriam Tavares at the local AGK brokerage in Sao Paulo.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased its purchases of dollars at daily spot market auctions over recent weeks.  \par \par \uc2 The bank doesn't disclose the volume of dollars bought at each auction but it accepted an elevated number of offers on Thursday. On Wednesday at a similar auction, the bank purchased $730 million, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has wielded a strong hand in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since the real broke the key resistance level of BRL2.10 per dollar in early February. The real had traded between BRL2.10 and BRL2.20 to the dollar for most of the last six months.  \par \par \uc2 Domestically, the benign inflation outlook continues. Early Friday, the Getulio Vargas Foundation reported that the IPC-S inflation index registered price rises of 0.43% in the thirty days up to Feb. 22, down from 0.54% in the thirty days up to Feb. 15. The result was within the forecast range of 0.37% to 0.56%.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release current account data for January at 1230 GMT. A survey of 16 analysts, conducted by the local Estado newswire, forecast a deficit of $1 billion to a surplus of $500 million. The current account is expected to show a surplus of $7.28 billion in 2007, according to a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey of analysts. In 2006, the current account surplus was $13.53 billion.  \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart; Dow Jones Newswires; 5511 3145-1479; alastair.stewart@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 02-23-07 0642ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070223e32n0011j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
