\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks finish at record but  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  slips  \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2007\par 14:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 22 (Reuters) - Brazil's stock market hit a record high on Thursday for the second straight session, while the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened slightly from its strongest level in nine months.  \par \par \uc2 The Bovespa index <.BVSP> of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange finished up 0.79 percent at 46,452 points after briefly touching a new intraday high of 46,752.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the index closed above the 46,000-point mark for the first time as foreign investors poured cash into emerging market assets, looking for bigger returns than those available in the United States or Europe.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> started out stronger for the third straight session but ended 0.24 percent weaker at 2.083 per U.S. dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy greenbacks to build foreign reserves.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's low inflation rate, rising international reserves, large trade surplus and high benchmark interest rate of 13 percent are attracting large inflows of dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have done little to rein in the hard-charging real, whose rally is worrying exporters and business leaders. They fear the strong exchange rate is making Brazilian products less competitive on world markets.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's stocks gained on Thursday even as official data showed that the country's jobless rate shot up to 9.3 percent in January from 8.4 percent in December, when unemployment tumbled to a one-year low because of seasonal hirings for the Christmas holiday.  \par \par \uc2 In the stock market, blue chips like state-run oil company Petrobras and mining giant CVRD helped drive the Bovespa higher. Both stocks are investor favorites.  \par \par \uc2 Petrobras , the heaviest-weighted stock in the index, rose 1.69 percent to 45.05 reais, while CVRD gained 1.01 percent to 66.04 reais.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070222e32m001cg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
