\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Weaker On Heavy Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2007\par 19:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 22, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 By Jeff Fick  \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Thursday after a spot-market dollar auction by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at a BRL2.082 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F, weaker from Wednesday's close of BRL2.077 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to act aggressively in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, snapping up dollars in a spot market auction called late in the session.  \par \par \uc2 The bank bought dollars in the snap auction for BRL2.077 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The real was trading at BRL2.0772 shortly before the auction was announced at 1724 GMT. The real traded weaker at BRL2.079 shortly after results of the auction were announced at 1734 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The bank didn't disclose the volume of dollars purchased.  \par \par \uc2 The auction followed a similar moves by the bank in recent weeks, which have resulted in mass purchases of dollars in an effort to stem the real's appreciation. On Wednesday at a similar auction, the bank purchased $730 million, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has wielded a strong hand in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since the real broke the key resistance level of BRL2.10 per dollar in early February. The real had traded between BRL2.10 and BRL2.20 to the dollar for most of the last six months.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, investors continue to expect further reductions in the Selic base interest rate after rates on bonds sold by the Brazilian Treasury declined in an auction Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian Treasury sold all $10.3 billion worth of bonds on offer at Thursday's auction at mostly lower rates than similar auctions held in late January and mid-February.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  next meets on March 7, when it is expected to cut the benchmark Selic base rate by as much as 50 basis points. The Selic base rate currently stands at 13.0%.  \par \par \uc2 Local interest rate futures tracked the trend, trading mostly lower during the session. However, the most actively traded local interest rate futures contract, April 2007, closed flat at 12.73%.  \par \par \uc2 The contracts project probable annualized interest charges for the overnight interbank rate at future dates.  \par \par \uc2 The actual overnight interbank rate for Thursday was 12.91%, up from Wednesday's close of 12.89%.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the risk to investing in Brazil as measured by the JP Morgan Emerging Market Bond Index Plus tightened slightly to a record-low spread of 175 basis points over U.S. Treasurys as of 1822 GMT. The benchmark Brazil 2040 bond was down 1/8 at 133 7/8 bid.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1481; jeff.fick@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 02-22-07 1337ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070222e32m002cg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
