\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil to add reserves while liquidity high-cenbank  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Walter Brandimarte  \par \uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2007\par 18:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Feb 16 (Reuters) - Brazil's policy of building foreign reserves should continue as long as global imbalances support a steady flow of dollars into the country, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director Paulo Vieira da Cunha said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think we will be building up reserves for 10 years ... but we are comfortable with our policy right now," Vieira da Cunha, who heads the international affairs department at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told analysts in New York.  \par \par \uc2 He explained that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like many other countries, keeps \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to counteract the effect of "global imbalances" caused by a mismatch in world interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 Low interest rates in the United States, Japan and Europe create carry trade opportunities, allowing investors to borrow in low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to invest in emerging countries like Brazil.  \par \par \uc2 As a result, Brazilian foreign reserves hit an all-time high of $95.9 billion on Wednesday. They are expected to keep growing as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to buy dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to dry up excess liquidity and, indirectly, prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating further.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts, the Brazilian real <BRBY> has been trading close to nine-month highs, raising complaints from the industrial sector.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are costly because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to offset them by selling bonds in the local market, in order to drain the excess of reais resulting from the buying of dollars.  \par \par \uc2 But Vieira da Cunha said that "rather than looking at domestic issues," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  focuses on global liquidity conditions to decide whether to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 He acknowledged that one of the costs of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a delay in a planned reduction of the stock of Brazil's local floating-rate debt, or LFTs.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian Treasury intends to cut as much as possible the share of public debt indexed to the country's base Selic rate. But the paper is the most efficient instrument the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to offset the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Vieira da Cunha said.  \par \par \uc2 "The Treasury would have reduced its stock of LFT much faster if it did not agree with our policy of sterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because it knows we need this kind of paper," he said.  \par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-ECONOMY/RESERVES|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070216e32g001r3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
