\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Weaker After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2007\par 19:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real closed slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar Thursday as investors tried to gauge the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases at an auction held late in the trading day.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.093 to the dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange after ending at BRL2.092 per dollar Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased the volumes of dollars bought in the daily auctions in recent days, holding the recent rise of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  partially in check.  \par \par \uc2 However, traders were unsure about the extent of the dollar purchases at Thursday's auction, conducted late in trade.  \par \par \uc2 The real was trading slightly stronger for most of the day until the auction.  \par \par \uc2 The market reacted little to the testimony of Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke before a committee of the House of Representatives in Washington, since he repeated testimony that was given to a Senate committee Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. economic figures, released earlier in the day, also had little impact on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Locally, the latest inflation data showed price rises remain benign.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's General Price Index, known as the IGP-M, rose 0.13% in the Jan. 21 to Feb. 10 period, compared with an increase of 0.32% seen in the Dec. 21 to Jan. 10 period. The slowdown in inflation was prompted by a deceleration in wholesale and consumer prices.  \par \par \uc2 Local interest rate futures were mostly lower during the session. The most actively traded local interest rate futures contract, January 2008, closed lower at 12.09%, down from Wednesday's close of 12.13%, on the benign local inflation outlook and declining U.S. Treasury note rates.  \par \par \uc2 The contracts project probable annualized interest charges for the overnight interbank rate at future dates.  \par \par \uc2 The actual overnight interbank rate for Thursday was flat at 12.88%.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the risk to investing in Brazil as measured by the JP Morgan Emerging Market Bond Index Plus widened slightly to a spread of 181 basis points over U.S. Treasurys as of 1825 GMT. The benchmark Brazil 2040 bond was down 3/10 at 133 7/10 bid.  \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart; Dow Jones Newswires; 5511 3145-1479; alastair.stewart@dowjones.com [ 15-02-07 1847GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070215e32f0010h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
