\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Weaker On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2007\par 12:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 13, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real opened slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to soak up inflowing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL2.115 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F, weaker from Monday's close of BRL2.113 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Late Monday, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would sell the equivalent of $450 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts at an auction Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced the sale to allow investors to roll over previously purchased reverse swaps.  \par \par \uc2 The auctions allow investors to swap \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions for government paper linked to interest rates. The interest rate paper is considered safer and less volatile. Typically, the auctions help support the U.S. dollar against the Brazilian real by removing real exposure from the market.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  forcefully on the spot market, buying increased amounts of dollars at daily auctions. The purchases have boosted the dollar in recent sessions after the real broke the key resistance level of BRL2.10 per dollar in early February. The real had traded between BRL2.10 and BRL2.20 to the dollar for most of the last six months.  \par \par \uc2 Investors will be looking at key economic data due to be released in the U.S. later in the day. U.S. trade balance data are scheduled at 1330 GMT and Redbook figures are due at 1355 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart; Dow Jones Newswires; 5511 3145-1479; alastair.stewart@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 02-13-07 0648ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070213e32d0010s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
