\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil stocks rise as CVRD, Arcelor gain; real up  \b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2007\par 15:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 13 (Reuters) - Brazilian stocks had their biggest one-day surge in over two months on Tuesday, lifted by shares of miner CVRD and steelmaker Arcelor Brasil, while \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained after a small \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Bovespa <.BVSP> index of the Sao Paulo Stock Exchange rose 2.87 percent to close at 45,197.45 points, its biggest gain since rising 3.2 percent on Dec. 4 . The real <BRBY> gained 0.24 percent to 2.109 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The real gained even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $452.1 million worth of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to roll over a similar batch of paper maturing on March 1. The swaps were originally sold to prevent the real from gaining too much.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars on the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market once again, though traders said it snapped up fewer dollars than in previous sessions.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has intensified purchases of dollars since the real hit a nine-month high last week, seeking to build up foreign reserves and, indirectly, blunt the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains. The bank's strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the past four sessions pushed the real 1.4 percent lower in the period.  \par \par \uc2 "It seems the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accepted fewer offers (in the auction," said Mario Battistel, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at the brokerage Novacao.  \par \par \uc2 On the stock market, iron ore miner CVRD rose 3.63 percent to close at 61.73 reais. Merrill Lynch said in a report on Tuesday it had increased by 24 percent the target price on CVRD's U.S.-traded shares to $42 from $34 on optimism over cost cuts and higher-than-expected iron ore prices.  \par \par \uc2 CVRD also said rating company Standard and Poor's affirmed its bond rating and removed a negative watch on the debt.  \par \par \uc2 Arcelor Brasil surged 12.4 percent to close at 47.6 reais, after trading on its shares was briefly suspended at the request of Brazil's securities regulator. The regulator ordered Arcelor Mittal , the world's largest steelmaker, to raise the price for the shares of its Brazilian unit that it does not already own. For details see [ID:nN13500434].  \par \par \uc2 Oil giant Petrobras gained 1.83 percent to 45.06 reais on a rise in oil prices after closing on Monday at its lowest since Jan. 18. The company reported on Tuesday a 36 percent slump in fourth-quarter profit to 5.2 billion reais and proposed dividend payments of 7.9 billion reais.  \par \par \uc2 Banco Itau Holding Financeira , Brazil's second-largest private sector bank, slipped 0.13 percent to close at 76.4 reais per share. The bank said on Tuesday fourth-quarter net income fell 10.5 percent to 1.28 billion reais, after taking a charge for its acquisition of Bank of America Corp.'s units in Chile and Uruguay.  \par \par \uc2 The bank also changed its dividend payment policy, representing an 18 percent gain for shareholders.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070213e32d001ih\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
