\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Weaker On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2007\par 12:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Feb 09, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 By Alastair Stewart  \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real opened weaker against the U.S. dollar Friday amid heavy dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  during its daily auctions in recent days.  \par \par \uc2 The real stood at BRL2.10 per dollar in early spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F, weaker from Thursday's close of BRL2.093 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has significantly increased the amount of dollars purchased during auctions over the last two days. According to traders, the bank bought $1.1 billion at auctions on Wednesday and Thursday, which is well above the daily average of $231 million in January.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased the purchases because of political pressure from President Luiz Inacio da Silva's administration, which is concerned about the affect of a strengthening real on exports and job creation.  \par \par \uc2 Last week, the Brazilian real broke the BRL2.10 barrier after trading between BRL2.10 and BRL2.20 for most of the last six months.  \par \par \uc2 However, traders said the dollar purchases could have a reverse effect in the medium term. That's because the purchases bolster foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which reduces Brazil's vulnerability to international market volatility and can cause increased dollar inflows.  \par \par \uc2 The pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do more about the strong real has led to market speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique Meirelles will resign. Meirelles and other ministers have denied the rumors.  \par \par \uc2 The local market is assessing the January IPCA inflation figures released by the Brazilian Census Bureau, or IBGE, on Friday morning.  \par \par \uc2 The IBGE said IPCA inflation totaled 0.44% in January, slowing from 0.48% in December. Twelve-month inflation fell to 2.99% in January from 3.14% in December. The benign inflation outlook leaves space for the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to reduce rates, as it has been doing for over a year. The base Selic interest rate currently stands at 13.00%.  \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart; Dow Jones Newswires; 5511 3145-1479; alastair.stewart@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 02-09-07 0647ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070209e329001be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
