\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Weaker On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alastair Stewart  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2007\par 19:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to buy dollars in larger volumes during the daily spot market auctions.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.108 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F, weaker from Thursday's close of BRL2.093 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has significantly increased the amount of dollars purchased during auctions since Wednesday. According to traders, the bank bought $1.1 billion at auctions on Wednesday and Thursday, which is well above the daily average of $231 million in January. The volume bought Friday was very similar to the previous two days, said one Sao Paulo trader.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased the purchase levels following political pressure from President Luiz Inacio da Silva's administration, which is concerned about the affect of a strengthening real on exports and job creation.  \par \par \uc2 However, speaking in Lisbon, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique Meirelles denied that the government has a target level or trading band for its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Local news reports said the political pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do more about the exchange rate has caused Meirelles to consider resignation. Meirelles has denied the reports.  \par \par \uc2 The latest Brazilian inflation data continued to paint a benign picture. The January IPCA inflation figures released by the Brazilian Census Bureau, or IBGE, totaled 0.44%, slowing from 0.48% in December. Twelve-month inflation fell to 2.99% in January from 3.14% in December. The benign inflation outlook leaves space for the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to reduce rates, as it has been doing for over a year. The base Selic interest rate currently stands at 13.00%.  \par \par \uc2 Local interest rate futures were mostly lower during the session. The most actively traded local interest rate futures contract, April 2007, closed at 12.76%, down from 12.78% on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The contracts project probable annualized interest charges for the overnight interbank rate at future dates.  \par \par \uc2 The actual overnight interbank rate for Friday was 12.89%, down from 12.90% on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart; Dow Jones Newswires; 5511 3145-1479; alastair.stewart@dowjones.com [ 09-02-07 1833GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1156 1843  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070209e329001k3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
