\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's stocks end higher,  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  stable  \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2007\par 16:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 8 (Reuters) - Brazilian stocks rose on Thursday, buoyed by a rise in shares of the country's biggest wireless company and state-controlled oil company, while the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged lower on increased \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Sao Paulo Stock Exchange's benchmark Bovespa index <.BVSP> rose 0.68 percent to close at 44,891.9 points, bouncing back from a loss on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> lost 0.05 percent to 2.094 per U.S. dollar, finishing almost unchanged from Wednesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market daily to buy dollars for \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves and, indirectly, to prevent the real from strengthening too much.  \par \par \uc2 Exporters have called on the government to do more to weaken the real to help their foreign sales, though Finance Minister Guido Mantega has discarded taking artificial measures to change the real's course.  \par \par \uc2 "Maybe the market is feeling a bit of pressure on the political side in relation to the exchange rate, so the market is betting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't let it strengthen too much," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a domestic brokerage who didn't want to be named.  \par \par \uc2 At the stock market, oil giant Petrobras rose 1.54 percent to 45.60 reais, leading the Bovespa higher as international crude prices jumped amid signs of falling exports from producer group OPEC. Petrobras, the heaviest stock in the index, gained after oil prices surged 3.4 percent in New York and 3.1 percent in London.  \par \par \uc2 Vivo Participacoes , Brazil's biggest wireless company, gained 6.12 percent to 8.84 reais. The company posted its first quarterly profit on Thursday after six consecutive quarters of losses by taking advantage of tax credits at a unit.  \par \par \uc2 Braskem , Latin America's largest petrochemical company, rose 1.79 percent to 15.37 reais. The company said on Thursday its fourth-quarter net income jumped to 78 million reais from 2 million reais a year earlier as the stronger Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  made it cheaper to pay foreign debt.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BRAZIL (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070208e328001xw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
