\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Weaker On Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2007\par 19:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Feb 08, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 By Jeff Fick  \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real closed weaker against the U.S. dollar Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the real's recent strength.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at a BRL2.0935 per dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, or BM&F, weaker from Thursday's close of BRL2.092 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 As investors expected, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market late in Thursday's session. The bank bought U.S. dollars in the spot market at a snap auction for BRL2.0937 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real was trading at BRL2.095 per dollar shortly after the bank announced the auction at 1722 GMT. The real traded weaker at BRL2.096 per dollar after results of the auction were announced at 1731 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The bank did not disclose the volume of dollars purchased.  \par \par \uc2 The auction followed a similar move by the bank Wednesday, when it purchased a larger-than-normal $550 million in a dollar purchase auction. In addition, the dollar quote set as the cutoff point for accepted bids was set higher than the spot-market dollar price at the time of the auction, as opposed to lower than the spot-market price at previous auctions.  \par \par \uc2 The move boosted the dollar, and market participants had expected a similar action Thursday after the real broke key resistance at BRL2.10 last week. The real had traded between BRL2.10 and BRL2.20 to the dollar for most of the last six months.  \par \par \uc2 Local interest rate futures were mostly lower during the session. The most actively traded local interest rate futures contract, January 2009, closed even with Wednesday's close of 12.14%.  \par \par \uc2 The contracts project probable annualized interest charges for the overnight interbank rate at future dates.  \par \par \uc2 The actual overnight interbank rate for Thursday was 12.90%, also even with Wednesday's close.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the risk to investing in Brazil as measured by the JP Morgan Emerging Market Bond Index Plus tightened slightly to a spread of 185 basis points over U.S. Treasurys as of 1800 GMT. The benchmark Brazil 2040 bond was up 1/8 at 132 7/8 bid.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1481; jeff.fick@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 02-08-07 1326ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070208e328002fz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
