\par\par \b \uc2 =  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Weaker On Possible Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2007\par 12:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 08, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real opened weaker against the U.S. dollar Thursday on expectations for more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and ahead of interest rate decisions overseas.  \par \par \uc2 The real opened at BRL2.094 per dollar in trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, weaker from Wednesday's close of BRL2.092.  \par \par \uc2 According to traders, the real is likely to trend weaker in Thursday's session because of expectations that the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be more aggressive in its daily dollar purchase auctions.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the bank purchased a larger-than-normal $550 million in its dollar purchase auction, traders said. In addition, the dollar quote set as the cutoff point for accepted bids was set higher than the spot-market dollar price at the time of the auction, as opposed to lower than the spot-market price at previous auctions.  \par \par \uc2 The move boosted the dollar, and market participants expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue to take similar actions to stem the real's recent strength. The real broke key resistance at BRL2.10 last week after trading between BRL2.10 and BRL2.20 to the dollar for most of the last six months.  \par \par \uc2 Later Thursday, the Bank of England and European Union \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release decisions on interest rates, which could influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in Brazil. Rising interest rates in developed economies typically sap investments from emerging markets such as Brazil.  \par \par \uc2 The risk to investing in Brazil as measured by the JP Morgan Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus, or EMBI+, stood at a spread of 184 basis points over U.S. Treasurys. The benchmark Brazil Global 40 bond closed Wednesday at a bid of 132 3/4.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jeff Fick, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1481; jeff.fick@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 02-08-07 0631ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070208e3280014e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
