\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Weaker On Large Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2007\par 19:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Feb 07, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real closed weaker Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought U.S. dollars heavily on the spot market.  \par \par \uc2 The real closed at BRL2.092 to the dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange, compared with Tuesday's close at BRL2.085 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real was trading stable in afternoon trade before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted one of its daily dollar purchase auctions. Normally, the purchases have little impact on the exchange rate but the bank bought a larger-than-normal amount of dollars Wednesday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "The larger purchase was the trigger for some profit taking after the real's gain over the last week," said one Sao Paulo-based trader.  \par \par \uc2 The real strengthened in early trade after Finance Minister Guido Mantega late Tuesday ruled out the use of capital controls to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, curiosity continued to abound over the meeting held Tuesday among President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, Mantega and \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Henrique Meirelles to talk about the strong Brazilian real.  \par \par \uc2 "The meeting led to speculation that the pace of interest rate reductions may be accelerated and the real gave ground," said the Sao Paulo trader.  \par \par \uc2 The weakening of the real also had much to do with profit-taking after a recent run-up in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The real broke key resistance at BRL2.10 last week after trading between BRL2.10 and BRL2.20 to the dollar for most of the last six months.  \par \par \uc2 News that U.S. fourth-quarter nonfarm business-sector productivity came in lower than expected, at 3%, acted to ease inflationary fears there and reinforced idea that U.S. interest rates would remain stable.  \par \par \uc2 In local interest rate markets, rates on the most heavily futures traded contract, April 2007, fell to 12.78% from 12.79% at the previous close.  \par \par \uc2 Brazil's interbank overnight rate, meanwhile, fell to 12.91% from 12.92%.  \par \par \uc2 -By Alastair Stewart; Dow Jones Newswires; 5511 3145-1479; alastair.stewart@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 02-07-07 1339ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070207e327001zs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
