\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Ends Stronger Following Local Market Gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2006\par 21:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real came back from midday doldrums to end stronger against the dollar Monday as investment flowed into the country following a rally of local asset prices late in the session.  \par \par \uc2 The real ended at BRL2.138 to the dollar in spot contract trading on the Brazilian Mercantile and Futures Exchange after ending at BRL2.141 per dollar Friday. [ 23-10-06 1948GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Traders noted the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened early in the session amid declining oil prices and speculation that the U.S. Federal Reserve could be prompted to ease up on tight monetary policy over coming months on an improving outlook.  \par \par \uc2 That movement was neutralized later in the session, however, by press reports Monday that the Fed would likely hold on to tight rate policy amid continued concerns about inflation pressure.  \par \par \uc2 The real got a bump back up to early highs, though, as equities prices locally and abroad rallied on investor enthusiasm over third-quarter earnings reports, and flows of funds toward local assets surged.  \par \par \uc2 The real made its advance late in the session despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which entered the market buying an unspecified amount of dollars at a rate of BRL2.1390 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in local interest rate futures trading Monday, the rate on the most heavily traded futures contract, January 2008, eased to 13.23% from 13.24% at Friday's close. The interbank overnight rate rose to 13.62% from 13.61%.  \par \par \uc2 